"siri_failed" = "Couldn’t load this channel or guide. Open the app for details.";
"siri_help" = "On iPhone, Siri and Shortcuts can tune channels by name or number, read what’s on now and next, search the guide, open a channel guide, and pause, resume or stop playback. Include the app name in your request. Siri asks for the search text. Add a playlist and open the app once to import its guide. Answers use the imported guide. These actions also work without Apple Intelligence; onscreen channel context needs iOS 18.2 or later and system support.";
"siri_programme_help" = "Programmes are in Spotlight and Siri too. Search a show title from the Home screen, or ask Siri what is on and follow up about a programme: record it, set a reminder for it, or open it in the guide. With a guide row or the player on screen, Siri knows which programme you mean. In guide search, Smart filter turns a plain-words request like \"sports tonight after 8\" into filters using only the on-device model; nothing about your guide leaves the phone.";
"siri_shortcuts" = "Siri and Shortcuts";
"siri_tuning_help" = "Say Play Sky Mix in Accessible IPTV, Tune to Sky Mix in Accessible IPTV, or Watch Sky Mix in Accessible IPTV. Add a channel to Favourites or play it once so Siri learns its name. Provider prefixes and quality labels need not be spoken. If Siri does not recognise a channel, say Watch TV in Accessible IPTV, then give its name when asked; this searches the full live playlist. Allow Siri time to update. For a command without the app name, create a personal shortcut with Tune channel set to Sky Mix and name it Play Sky Mix, Tune to Sky Mix, or Watch Sky Mix.";
